StairVLA — provenance and licensing
===================================

StairVLA is built on StarVLA (https://github.com/starVLA/starVLA), which is
distributed under the MIT License. The StarVLA copyright notice and permission
notice are retained in LICENSE. The git history of this repository starts from
StarVLA commit 29f97a9; every StarVLA commit up to that point is preserved, and
the StairVLA changes are added on top.

1. Original to StairVLA
-----------------------
  starVLA/model/framework/HierarchicalVLA.py
      High-level policy wrapper, partial-denoising trajectory construction,
      flow-matching velocity target, chunk batching, and hierarchical inference
      with high-level trajectory reuse.
  starVLA/model/modules/action_model/Hierarchical_ActionHead.py
      Low-level refiner: cross-attention DiT, real-time observation encoder,
      high-level feature compression, temporal action context, masked loss.
  examples/LIBERO/train_files/*          (StairVLA configs and launchers)
  examples/LIBERO/eval_files/eval_libero_all.sh
  examples/LIBERO-plus/train_files/*
  examples/LIBERO-plus/eval_files/eval_libero_all.sh
  examples/PiperX/**                     (real-robot configs and data preparation)
  scripts/benchmark_latency.py

